	I'm sure this has been asked before but I haven't seen anything lately 
so I'll ask. How do people in this newsgroup feel about Slash 'em? I've 
never played it but I looked at the Slash 'em web site a little bit 
today. I saw some nice improvements over Nethack but I don't know how 
they play out in a real game. I've never even completed a quest in 
Nethack let alone ascending so I'm not even qualified to comment over 
most of the changes.
	Do you think Slash 'em is basically a better Nethack? Or is it 
worse/cheesy in some ways? What do you like/dislike about it? Do you 
think Slash 'em is a totally different game so it's not even comparable 
to plain vanilla Nethack? What would you recommend to a Nethack player 
who has never ascended: to keep playing Nethack until she ascends or 
drop Nethack and start playing Slash 'em?
	I assume many (if not all) of the changes in Slash 'em come from people 
who play Nethack very well and address any bugs/shortcomings as well as 
making the game more enjoyable. So it makes sense to think it should be 
better (especially given Nethack's slow release schedule).
	I guess it's kinda like a game vs. its community mods but in this case 
the mod is kind of standard and has a large user base.
	I'd want to hear opinions of Slash 'em fans and Nethack purists. What 
do you all think?


